{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1792483021","published":"2026-10-29T13:43:15Z","modified":"2026-11-27T16:43:47.658241662Z","upstream":["CVE-2007-4559","CVE-2024-12718","CVE-2025-4138","CVE-2025-4330","CVE-2025-4435","CVE-2025-4517","CVE-2026-11940","CVE-2026-19672","CVE-2026-4360","CVE-2026-7774","CVE-2026-82049","CVE-2026-87910"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2007-4559, CVE-2026-11940, CVE-2026-82049","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: Directory traversal in tarfile extraction\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2007-4559.patch: make the PEP 706 extraction filters\n       available for tarfile and shutil.unpack_archive, including the 'data'\n       filter that rejects members escaping the destination directory. The\n       filters are opt-in and the default extraction behaviour is unchanged\n       (still 'fully_trusted', i.e. no filtering), matching upstream Python\n       3.9. Callers must opt in explicitly, via\n       tar.extractall(path, filter='data') per call,\n       TarFile.extraction_filter = tarfile.data_filter process-wide, or\n       shutil.unpack_archive(..., filter='data'); include the upstream\n       gh-135034 through gh-157265 rollups so the opt-in filters normalize\n       link targets, re-filter link fallbacks and directory fixups, skip\n       rejected members when errorlevel is zero, and resolve hardlink targets.\n     - CVE-2007-4559\n     - CVE-2024-12718\n     - CVE-2025-4138\n     - CVE-2025-4330\n     - CVE-2025-4435\n     - CVE-2025-4517\n     - CVE-2026-4360\n     - CVE-2026-7774\n     - CVE-2026-11940\n     - CVE-2026-19672\n     - CVE-2026-82049\n     - CVE-2026-87910","affected":[{"package":{"name":"idle-python3.9","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:11","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/idle-python3.9?distro=debian-11"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.9.2-1+deb11u7+tuxcare.els4"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian11els/CLSA-2026-1792483021.json"}}